          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-c0e0cc2bb62bdba5\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.93,\"analysis\":\"Rodolphe’s repeated “Si je t’aime! si je t’aime!” is principally an emphatic avowal that presents his love as true. Because it answers Emma’s demand that he swear his love, it has weak oath-like or commitment force, but it does not clearly undertake a relational obligation. Repetition and exclamation intensify the avowal without independently establishing expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The oath-eliciting question gives some support to P, but Rodolphe answers with an intensified assertion rather than an explicit promise or oath.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Rodolphe directly addresses Emma; the classified event is his repeated reply “Si je t’aime! si je t’aime!” within the fuller declaration “mais je t’adore, mon amour!”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Emma asks “M’aimes-tu? Jure-le donc!”, making Rodolphe’s declaration a solicited reassurance on the eve of their planned flight. His prior delays, strange manner, and later hesitant responses cast contextual doubt on his sincerity and commitment, but deception or reluctance does not change the utterance’s dominant assertoric force. The romantic setting and emphatic repetition increase intensity, not E.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Emma asks, “M’aimes-tu? Jure-le donc!” and Rodolphe replies, “Si je t’aime! si je t’aime! mais je t’adore, mon amour!”\",\"supports\":\"The reply explicitly presents Rodolphe’s love as true, strongly supporting T; the request to swear supplies limited support for an oath-like P reading.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Before the declaration, Rodolphe has repeatedly delayed the planned flight and looks at Emma “singulièrement, d’une façon tendre.”\",\"supports\":\"His declaration occurs amid signs of hesitation, making possible insincerity or strategic reassurance contextually relevant without altering the core T/P classification.\",\"confidence\":0.92},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The declaration uses repetition and exclamation, but the narration does not describe the words as involuntary, blurted, or reflexively produced.\",\"supports\":\"Intensity is present, but there is no positive evidence for independent expressive/reflexive force, supporting E=0.\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the emphatic avowal, while a low P score registers the oath-eliciting setting. Delivery and narrative suspicion are adequately handled as context; no important core force remains outside T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
